  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output A.1. Enhanced decent work statistics using innovative sources and statistical standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.The Government of the Republic of Namibia, through the National Statistical Agency (NSA) has established a Labour Market Information System (LMIS). 
a. The (LMIS.Stat) Database tool for the storage and dissemination of indicators LMIS has been set-up and is now LIVE allowing for stakeholders in the national statistical system to update data and information on the labour market.
 1.The ILO has provided technical and financial support for including capacity building and technical backstopping services for the installation of the LMIS.Stat system at NSA. The following activities have been supported:
a. A Data Production Workshop was conducted to review labour market indicators (source, formula, definition, classification, disaggregation) for all data producers and users in the country in 2022.
b. The LMIS.Stat application software was installed at the NSA in 2022.
c. Trainings have been conducted for LMI officials focusing on IT, data and metadata.
d. Configuration of structural metadata and initial loading of data was undertaken in 2022 and workshop on SDMX and Data Modelling were conducted by the ILO in 2022.
e. NSA officials attended a special workshop conducted in Turin by ILO LMIS team, to support countries that are about to launch LMIS.</narrative>
   </description>
